{"ts":"2026-10-10T08:14:15.868Z","type":"agent_event","event":{"type":"content_end","contentType":"reasoning","reasoning":"The typecheck issue is that LayoutProps is a global type Next generates during build, so tsc doesn't recognize it beforehand; also the exit code echo in cmd is unreliable since it expands at parse time. I should switch to an explicit `{ children: React.ReactNode }` type with Readonly, which is the more conventional, build-independent approach.\n\nLint passes, but typecheck fails since `LayoutProps` only exists in `.next/types` after a dev/build run—I'll type `children` explicitly to avoid that dependency. Also switching my error-check approach from the unreliable `EXIT=%ERRORLEVEL%` echo to `&& echo OK || echo FAIL`.\n\n"}}
